  [  164.4-  165.9] and managing their risks.
  [  166.7-  171.9] And finally, an important gap that we've really begun to look
  [  171.9-  173.9] at since the crisis is
  [  173.9-  176.9] that with individual agencies looking at different parts
  [  176.9-  179.6] of the system, there was not enough attention being paid
  [  179.6-  182.1] to the stability of the financial system taken
  [  182.1-  182.7] as a whole.
  [  184.8-  186.3] Let me talk just a moment more
  [  186.3-  189.2] about another important public sector vulnerability
  [  189.8-  192.9] and these were the so-called government sponsored
  [  192.9-  194.7] enterprises, Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac.
  [  195.7-  198.1] Now, Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac are nominally private
